parameters.help_en:
The path of the import package file.
Note: This operation involves file uploads. The following example shows how to call this operation:

```java
        Config config = new Config();
        config.setAccessKeyId(accessId);
        config.setAccessKeySecret(accessKey);
        config.setEndpoint(popEndpoint);
        config.setRegionId(regionId);

        Client client = new Client(config);

        CreateImportMigrationAdvanceRequest request = new CreateImportMigrationAdvanceRequest();
        request.setName("test_migration_api_" + System.currentTimeMillis());
        request.setProjectId(123456L); 
        request.setPackageType("DATAWORKS_MODEL");
        request.setPackageFileObject(new FileInputStream("/home/admin/Downloads/test.zip"));

        RuntimeOptions runtime = new RuntimeOptions();
        CreateImportMigrationResponse response = client.createImportMigrationAdvance(request, runtime);
```

If you directly pass the file path, the parameter value must be a valid URL of an OSS object within the caller's account, such as https://{bucket}.oss-{region}.aliyuncs.com/{object_key}. Cross-account OSS URLs are rejected. If you use the SDK Advance method, you can upload the file by using a local file stream

